data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":596,"item_id":"msg_02e6351f68cd7f71016b031374462c87d1b2cfd3abef37a31f","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"actor\":\"ash-4\",\"decision\":\"reuse\",\"ability\":\"probe\",\"reason\":\"The implemented probe interface already supports non-ingestive physical testing of a small owned sample, separately from direct visual observation. Reuse it for the feasible preliminary investigation; no supplied capability or equipment establishes nutrition, toxicity or general food safety. A physical trial must report its actual observations and leave unsupported food-safety questions unresolved. Neither tasting nor feeding another participant is required or authorized.\",\"specification\":\"Use probe's existing physical-trial operation with the explicit owned sample item-32-ash-4-785. Validate current ownership, remaining quantity and the chosen supported trial before charging anything. Cost: one simulation round, 0.5 energy and 0.1 actual sample unit, as already implemented. Select only an executable non-ingestive material trial supported by probe; declare its method and any required actual implements before execution. If an implement is required but unavailable, fail without inventing equipment or results. Record the tested quantity, method, conditions, consumed sample provenance and observed result. A mechanical response or visible interior, if actually exposed by the supported trial, establishes only that observation—not nutrient content, absence of toxins or suitability for eating. If probe has no supported trial relevant beyond the existing observation, return that limitation without pretending to perform a food assay. Preserve the untested remainder, ownership and accumulated spoilage; do not convert testing into consumption or change nutrition, toxicity, health or hunger. Use the existing probe public schema and trial-result/trial-material-consumed events; retain existing atomic completion and failure behavior, with no new persistent process, escrow, objects or collision geometry. Implementation, individual learning and execution remain separate; this review advances no simulation time.\",\"experienceReview\":\"Application, study and an inconclusive attempt earn no feedback. If the performed trial actually confirms previously unresolved information, emit information-confirmed through probe with qualified=true and the actor as the sole beneficiary, using the existing grounded-understanding source—not a new alias. Its temporary feedback is 0.8, capped at 1, held for 8 rounds, refresh repetition and 12-round cooldown. Its maintained component gains 0.035 only on qualifying confirmation events and decays by 0.0015 under the existing rule. Repeated confirmation of the same fact does not qualify. Mechanical information can qualify as understanding without implying food safety; unsupported conclusions cannot. No separate pleasure, physical-comfort or health benefit is established by testing.\",\"visualReview\":\"Show the actual sample targeted, the performed trial, paid sample and energy costs, observed result, and remaining quantity in the existing probe event presentation and replay. Clearly distinguish measured observations from unresolved nutrition and toxicity. Do not display a safe-food badge, invented laboratory equipment or an eating animation. Any consumed fragment must disappear only through the recorded material debit; the remainder retains its actual world or inventory representation.\",\"learning\":0}]}","logprobs":[]}

